   "note": "Estimate. East of 1st Street the interchange ramps stand on the old plateau rim above Shockoe Valley. The USGS Richmond sheet surveyed 1933-34 shows ground there at about the height the lidar measures today (its 150-foot contour, labeled near the valley rim, falls where today's does), so the ground is kept as measured, except that banks narrower than 50 m (the ramps' embankments, up to 9 m high) are taken down to the ground beside them. The ravine the sheet shows heading into the plateau north of the junction, and the valley side under I-95 south of it, are not rebuilt: the lidar is kept there.",
